# linuxkpi component options.
#
# The observation switch is the one linuxkpi-side lever the old profiles
# carried; it is CFG_DEFS-only (CONFIG_LKPI_USB_OBS) in the generated
# fragment.  The WLAN_OBS switch that turns on the census lives in the
# wireless test config.

menu "linuxkpi"

config LKPI_USB_OBS
	bool "USB observation points"
	help
	  The linuxkpi USB submit/complete observation points.  It is a
	  diagnostic arm: the observation cost is part of the measured image,
	  so it is a profile decision, not a default.

config LKPI_JOIN_TRACE
	bool "join trace"
	help
	  Two lines per channel tune in the linuxkpi face (`wlan: tune begin` and
	  `wlan: tune done <MHz> rc=`), plus the driver-callback breadcrumbs the
	  join path runs through.  It answers "did the driver tune to the AP's
	  channel and with what result" from the console alone; the macro the
	  sources test is LKPI_JOIN_TRACE.

config LKPI_TXQ_AUDIT
	bool "transmit-queue engine invariant audit"
	help
	  Compares the engine's per-queue counter with the list the queue
	  actually links, at every engine exit (O(1) per call), and writes a
	  full slot dump the first few times the two disagree; it also counts
	  frames released while a queue still links them, slots reused with
	  frames still on them, and nodes left in slots whose txq is NULL.
	  This is the 2026-11-06 wedge's instrument: a boot that breaks names
	  its own first break instead of its final state.  Diagnostic arm
	  only - the comparison and the dump are part of the measured image.
	  The macro the sources test is CONFIG_LKPI_TXQ_AUDIT.

endmenu
